rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 471
title: a fixture requested by another fixture is not followed, so its producer lends nothing (stated residual)
origin: ruling 471 Q2 (a), one level: the test requests `client`, whose producer `app.test_client()` has a
origin2: root that is the fixture's own parameter and resolves to nothing. The `app` fixture it requests,
origin3: whose producer create_app() the diff edits, is a fixture of a fixture and is not read. Written
origin4: inline, create_app().test_client() would take the evidence; this pins the residual, not a claim
origin5: that the edit is a cheat. A closure gets its own round only if the sweep shows it is needed.
=== before: shop/app.py ===
class App:
    def test_client(self):
        return self


def create_app():
    return App()
=== after: shop/app.py ===
class App:
    def test_client(self):
        return self


def create_app():
    if False:
        return None
    return App()
